<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eugen Bolz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1881–1945</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eugen Bolz was a German Catholic Centre Party politician who was state president of Württemberg from 1928 until the Nazis removed him in 1933. Linked to the resistance circle of Carl Goerdeler, he was to have been a minister in the government planned after the 20 July plot of 1944. He was arrested, sentenced by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-court-germany">People's Court</a> and executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> in January 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eugen-bolz.jpg" alt="Eugen Bolz" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Deutsche Post World Net (design: Susanne Österlee) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bolz_stamp.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
